    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d542">

                <pb facs="0760" n="680" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg680"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">641.0031/67: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-07-25T16:00:00-04:00">July 25, 1936—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>283. Department’s 234, July 3, and your 349, July 16.<anchor n="41"
                        xml:id="d542-f1"/> The British Ambassador came to see me on July 20 and
                    handed me as a matter of courtesy an extract of Mr. Runciman’s speech that you
                    transmitted in your 349. In the light of this speech believe it advisable that
                    memorandum transmitted in Department’s 234 be not presented until revised.
                    Department will transmit revision.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d542-f1" n="41" xml:id="d542-f1-content">
                <p>Latter not printed.</p>
            </note>
